ion", "contents": [{"content": "enpe7n3le01ob09re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Data communication is easy as cake!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le01ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Dylan:</strong> Sure! I know that data communications refer to the transfer of information between computers and users as well. <br/>\n<strong>Kate:</strong> Yes. At the most abstract level, to make communication possible, data communications need two or more computers, a device to turn information into electronic signals, and a transmission medium.<br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "22000", "text": "<strong>Dylan:</strong> Don't forget it also needs a software that manages the flow of information. What are the devices that transform information?<br/>\n<strong>Kate:</strong> Well, I'm checking that part. They're called modems. This communication can happen in different ways, from telephones to wireless connections. I'm just trying to understand how data communications works. <br/>\n<strong>Dylan:</strong> When the computers are not connected, the data travels through a network (local or global). Because networks are wide, the data needs to travel with address and the place where it fits.<br/>\n<strong>Kate:</strong> Is it necessary to divide the information before the computer sends it?<br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "66000", "text": "<strong>Dylan:</strong> Yes. It makes the process easier. Is there anything else we can use for the test?<br/><strong>Kate:</strong> Of course! More specific features describe the serial transmission. It's when data transfer occurs one bit at a time. Different to multiplexed when it's possible to carry many channels with more bits at the same time. <br/>\n<strong>Dylan:</strong> Ok. I read that today, many different ways of transfer are working in different devices. For example, a single device can transfer data in different ways. Technology nowadays requires devices to be very flexible.<br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le01ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}